🔐 STIG Remediation: Restrict 'Back up files and directories' User Right

STIG ID: WN10-UR-000030 
Severity: Medium
SRG: SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048
CCI: CCI-000213
Vuln ID: V-XXXXX
Vulnerability Status: ✅ Active

📖 Overview

This STIG ensures that only authorized users — specifically the Administrators group — have the "Back up files and directories" user right. Misconfigured privileges can lead to unauthorized access to sensitive data by bypassing standard file and folder permissions.

⚠️ Why It Matters

Accounts with this right can circumvent NTFS file system permissions, potentially accessing or exfiltrating sensitive data. Limiting this capability reduces insider threat risk and minimizes lateral movement by threat actors.

🔍 Check: User Rights Assignment

Using GUI:

Open the Local Security Policy tool:

Press Win + R, type secpol.msc, and press Enter.

Navigate to:

Computer Configuration >>
Windows Settings >>
Security Settings >>
Local Policies >>
User Rights Assignment

Locate the policy:

Back up files and directories

Confirm it only includes:

Administrators

❌ If any other groups or users (e.g., Backup Operators, Users) are listed, this is a finding.


Using PowerShell:

secedit /export /cfg C:\temp\sec.cfg
Select-String "SeBackupPrivilege" C:\temp\sec.cfg

Output should include only *S-1-5-32-544 (SID for Administrators group).


🛠️ Remediation Steps

Open secpol.msc

Navigate to:
Local Policies → User Rights Assignment

Double-click Back up files and directories

Remove all entries except Administrators

Click Apply → OK


🔄 Reboot Required?

Yes. To ensure the change takes effect:

Reboot the system (preferred), or

Log off and back in


📎 Notes

The Backup Operators group is often added by default in some systems — remove it unless explicitly required and documented.

Although this remediation was performed on Windows 10, the same guidance applies to Windows 11 under STIG ID: WN11-UR-000030.
